00:13:34.797 --> 00:13:37.800
Pretty good.
(audience laughing)

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:40.660
Before the first part of the video clips,

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:45.590
we thought we would set the
mood with "The Way We Were,"

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:49.140
a tune from the 1973 romantic drama

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.670
starring Barbara Streisand
and Robert Redford.

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:55.810
To sing it for us, we have Sara Speller.

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:58.490
Sara graduated from Yale last May

00:13:58.490 --> 00:14:00.160
and is about to leave for England

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:02.420
to take up a fellowship to pursue

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:05.820
an Mphil in Musicology at Oxford.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.440
She will be accompanied today

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:11.580
by Mahima Humara from the Class of 2020,

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.940
an accomplished pianist,
who has received awards

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:18.440
at the Duquesne Young
Artist National Competition

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.620
and the Pennsylvania Music Teachers

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:23.060
National Association Competition.

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:27.530
She's a member of Yale's
Undergraduate Piano Collective.

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:30.580
The song will be followed by the montage

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:35.480
from a few of the 100 or so
voices we've captured thus far

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:39.770
about those first days and
weeks and months at Yale,

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:42.790
especially the challenges that came

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:46.900
with breaking a barrier
more than 250 years old

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.993
at an entrenched patriarchal institution.

00:14:49.993 --> 00:14:51.140
(audience laughing)

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:54.134
And now, Sara and Mahima.

00:14:54.134 --> 00:14:57.301
(audience applauding)

