♪ Some day ♪
♪ Day day some day ♪

01:07:50.281 --> 01:07:55.281
♪ Oh, deep in my heart ♪
♪ Deep in my heart ♪

01:07:59.894 --> 01:08:04.894
♪ I do believe ♪

01:08:07.627 --> 01:08:12.627
♪ We shall overcome ♪

01:08:13.095 --> 01:08:15.345
♪ Some day ♪

01:08:23.764 --> 01:08:26.514
♪ Shall overcome ♪

01:08:29.696 --> 01:08:33.946
(audience cheering and applauding)

01:09:13.040 --> 01:09:16.360
- We are welcoming the
Class of 2023 right now,

01:09:16.360 --> 01:09:18.760
and it's so wonderful
to have an opportunity

01:09:18.760 --> 01:09:23.397
to take a break and think
about the women of '69 to '73,

01:09:23.397 --> 01:09:27.150
the people who actually led
the charge to come to Yale

01:09:27.150 --> 01:09:29.820
to make it a place for
all of us to come to.

01:09:29.820 --> 01:09:32.470
Thank you so much for everything you did

01:09:32.470 --> 01:09:34.110
when you were here as a student,

01:09:34.110 --> 01:09:37.000
for the many things you
do as alumni of Yale.

01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:40.530
And I just wanna salute your
courage, your curiosity,

01:09:40.530 --> 01:09:43.340
and thank you for taking that
first step for all of us.

01:09:43.340 --> 01:09:46.850
- I wanna say thank you to the
first female students at Yale

01:09:46.850 --> 01:09:50.310
for making it possible when
I was a student in the '90s

01:09:50.310 --> 01:09:51.980
to feel like it was completely normal

01:09:51.980 --> 01:09:53.650
for me to be on campus.

01:09:53.650 --> 01:09:55.050
I now have the privilege of being the

01:09:55.050 --> 01:09:56.630
Dean of Jonathan Edwards College,

01:09:56.630 --> 01:09:58.910
and I see my female students occupying

01:09:58.910 --> 01:10:00.840
leadership roles across campus.

01:10:00.840 --> 01:10:03.540
It wouldn't be possible
without you so thank you.

01:10:03.540 --> 01:10:06.870
- I have looked up to so
many of you for so long.

01:10:06.870 --> 01:10:09.160
You include my heroines.

01:10:09.160 --> 01:10:11.560
I feel as if I have personally stood

01:10:11.560 --> 01:10:14.010
on the shoulders of so many of you.

01:10:14.010 --> 01:10:16.560
I so hope this weekend has been memorable

01:10:16.560 --> 01:10:17.810
and a little provocative.

01:10:17.810 --> 01:10:21.510
My prayer is that something
during your time back

01:10:21.510 --> 01:10:24.540
has seized your heart and will engage you

01:10:24.540 --> 01:10:27.490
to come back often to
Yale in the coming years.

01:10:27.490 --> 01:10:29.120
Bravo and thank you.

01:10:29.120 --> 01:10:30.810
- The courage of one generation

01:10:30.810 --> 01:10:34.360
makes possible the
accomplishments of the next.

01:10:34.360 --> 01:10:36.540
We're grateful to inhabit the world

01:10:36.540 --> 01:10:38.257
whose doors you opened.

01:10:39.270 --> 01:10:40.103
Thank you.

01:10:40.103 --> 01:10:44.440
- Kudos to the bold women of
Yale's first co-ed classes.

01:10:44.440 --> 01:10:47.450
You challenged Yale to learn from you.

01:10:47.450 --> 01:10:50.110
You made Yale better for the future.

01:10:50.110 --> 01:10:52.770
And you inspired by your leadership

01:10:52.770 --> 01:10:55.970
those who came after
you, including myself.

01:10:55.970 --> 01:10:59.030
I was Yale's first women General Counsel

01:10:59.030 --> 01:11:01.510
and served for 30 years.

01:11:01.510 --> 01:11:04.730
Thank you for all you've done
for Yale and for the world.

01:11:04.730 --> 01:11:06.520
- At the school of architecture,

01:11:06.520 --> 01:11:10.370
Minerva presides over our design studios.

01:11:10.370 --> 01:11:12.340
How wonderful is it that the

01:11:12.340 --> 01:11:16.220
goddess of wisdom is our inspiration.

01:11:16.220 --> 01:11:18.600
In that spirit, I'd like to thank

01:11:18.600 --> 01:11:20.640
the women who came to Yale in the classes

01:11:20.640 --> 01:11:25.640
of 1969 through 1973 for all
they brought to the university.

01:11:26.490 --> 01:11:29.910
Bravo to you, goddesses
of wisdom, and thank you.

01:11:29.910 --> 01:11:31.611
(audience laughing)

01:11:31.611 --> 01:11:33.770
- That is what every woman
in the Yale Law School

01:11:33.770 --> 01:11:37.470
building feels about the
generations that came before us.

01:11:37.470 --> 01:11:40.090
I'm the first female
dean of Yale Law School.

01:11:40.090 --> 01:11:43.551
This incoming class is 54% women.

01:11:43.551 --> 01:11:46.510
(audience cheering and applauding)

01:11:46.510 --> 01:11:47.980
Thank you for blazing the trails

01:11:47.980 --> 01:11:51.220
and smoothing the path and
making all of this possible.

01:11:51.220 --> 01:11:52.830
We are in your debt.

01:11:52.830 --> 01:11:56.160
- I'm Daisy Mazzio-Manson, a
Senior here at Yale University.

01:11:56.160 --> 01:11:59.010
In 1999 my mom made a film
called "A Hero for Daisy,"

01:11:59.010 --> 01:12:01.860
which is a documentary
focusing on Chris Ernst

01:12:01.860 --> 01:12:04.340
whose a Title IX pioneer and Olympian,

01:12:04.340 --> 01:12:07.110
who led the 1976 Yale women's crew team

01:12:07.110 --> 01:12:09.300
to protest the lack of facilities

01:12:09.300 --> 01:12:11.000
available for female athletes.

01:12:11.000 --> 01:12:13.640
Today, I'm a rower on the
Yale women's crew team,

01:12:13.640 --> 01:12:15.220
where we have exceptional facilities

01:12:15.220 --> 01:12:17.050
and an elite coaching staff who work

01:12:17.050 --> 01:12:20.250
to provide us with all the
resources we need to excel.

01:12:20.250 --> 01:12:22.350
I'm so thankful for the
women who came before me

01:12:22.350 --> 01:12:25.050
and fought so hard for the
opportunities that we have today.

01:12:25.050 --> 01:12:28.180
- Hi, Joliana Yee, and I just want

01:12:28.180 --> 01:12:31.480
to extend the deepest
of gratitude and thanks

01:12:31.480 --> 01:12:34.040
to the first women at Yale for,

01:12:34.040 --> 01:12:35.970
because of your perseverance,

01:12:35.970 --> 01:12:38.170
I'm allowed to stand here before you

01:12:38.170 --> 01:12:41.200
as the Director of the Asian
American Cultural Center.

01:12:41.200 --> 01:12:43.830
And especially a big shout
out to the women of color

01:12:43.830 --> 01:12:45.470
because I know it wasn't easy.

01:12:45.470 --> 01:12:47.010
Congratulations and thank you.

01:12:47.010 --> 01:12:51.320
- I am so grateful for the women
at Yale who came before us.

01:12:51.320 --> 01:12:54.640
It takes bravery, courage,
their love for Yale

01:12:54.640 --> 01:12:58.310
to do what you've done,
and I'm a product of that.

01:12:58.310 --> 01:13:00.710
And so, I'm so grateful and thankful

01:13:00.710 --> 01:13:03.930
for the women at Yale
to bring in inclusivity,

01:13:03.930 --> 01:13:07.170
leadership, bravery, and love.

01:13:07.170 --> 01:13:09.630
Thank you, thank you so much.

01:13:09.630 --> 01:13:12.470
- I simply can't imagine either my classes

01:13:12.470 --> 01:13:15.640
or the colleges without all
the wonderful young women

01:13:15.640 --> 01:13:17.760
I've come to know there.

01:13:17.760 --> 01:13:22.330
Thanks so much to the women
of the classes of '69 to '73

01:13:22.330 --> 01:13:25.290
for taking the big leap
and making it all possible.

01:13:25.290 --> 01:13:27.450
- I want to take this opportunity

01:13:27.450 --> 01:13:30.810
to thank the women who
arrived on the Yale campus

01:13:30.810 --> 01:13:35.810
in the fall of 1969 to
transform this university.

01:13:36.020 --> 01:13:38.740
For had you not made the change

01:13:38.740 --> 01:13:42.320
of making Yale a place
that welcomed women,

01:13:42.320 --> 01:13:44.410
Yale could not have become the

01:13:44.410 --> 01:13:47.250
great university that it would become

01:13:47.250 --> 01:13:51.270
in the last quarter of the 20th century.

01:13:51.270 --> 01:13:52.103
Thank you.

01:13:52.103 --> 01:13:55.350
- As someone following only
a few years behind you,

01:13:55.350 --> 01:13:58.940
and as a woman in the
male-dominated field of physics,

01:13:58.940 --> 01:14:02.750
I know exactly how important
you are as path breakers.

01:14:02.750 --> 01:14:06.160
You led the most important
change in Yale's history.

01:14:06.160 --> 01:14:08.753
So, thank you so much.

01:14:08.753 --> 01:14:10.810
- What a long way Yale has come

01:14:10.810 --> 01:14:13.640
since I arrived here in 1972 as a

01:14:13.640 --> 01:14:16.150
newly mentored assistant professor.

01:14:16.150 --> 01:14:18.270
It's good, and it's right that we

01:14:18.270 --> 01:14:20.467
should celebrate, and I do.

01:14:20.467 --> 01:14:23.247
But you know, there's still a ways to go.

01:14:23.247 --> 01:14:26.010
(audience laughing)

01:14:26.010 --> 01:14:28.300
- I follow in the
footsteps that you paved.

01:14:28.300 --> 01:14:30.630
Thanks to you, the first
class of Yale women,

01:14:30.630 --> 01:14:33.780
for your resiliency, strength, and poise.

01:14:33.780 --> 01:14:36.300
Thanks to you, I too am Yale.

01:14:36.300 --> 01:14:38.570
- To our pioneers, our first classes

01:14:38.570 --> 01:14:41.550
of women at Yale College, we salute you.

01:14:41.550 --> 01:14:42.980
We honor you.

01:14:42.980 --> 01:14:45.780
Countless women and people
of all genders at Yale

01:14:45.780 --> 01:14:47.530
and beyond are indebted to you

01:14:47.530 --> 01:14:51.160
for blazing these paths
with such brilliance,

01:14:51.160 --> 01:14:53.450
courage, grace, and tenacity.

01:14:53.450 --> 01:14:55.313
Thank you, and happy anniversary.

01:14:57.397 --> 01:15:00.564
(audience applauding)

01:15:08.062 --> 01:15:10.160
- Thank you to everyone who contributed

01:15:10.160 --> 01:15:12.670
to that wonderful, wonderful video,

01:15:12.670 --> 01:15:15.720
which was really inspiring
and moving and gratifying

01:15:15.720 --> 01:15:18.640
to feel that all of this has developed

01:15:18.640 --> 01:15:23.640
from our initial steps here
back in 1969, '70 through '73.

01:15:25.800 --> 01:15:28.260
The following song, sung by Cami,

01:15:28.260 --> 01:15:29.890
is the one requested by the committee

01:15:29.890 --> 01:15:31.930
to be the finale of the day.

01:15:31.930 --> 01:15:33.740
It's a second song by Carole King,

01:15:33.740 --> 01:15:36.320
but that's not the
reason it was requested.

01:15:36.320 --> 01:15:39.270
The words represent to the
women who've requested it

01:15:39.270 --> 01:15:41.400
the bond that all of us share

01:15:41.400 --> 01:15:44.000
and the way we feel about one another.

01:15:44.000 --> 01:15:46.030
The song will be immediately followed

01:15:46.030 --> 01:15:49.240
by a brief closing
tribute by Kinsale Houston

01:15:49.240 --> 01:15:52.170
after which Kinsale
will ask us all to rise

01:15:52.170 --> 01:15:54.080
and sing "Bright College Years"

01:15:54.080 --> 01:15:56.719
led by the Yale Precision Marching Band.

01:15:56.719 --> 01:15:58.160
(audience laughing)

01:15:58.160 --> 01:16:00.300
After we finish the alma mater,

01:16:00.300 --> 01:16:03.240
please don't sit back down.

01:16:03.240 --> 01:16:05.340
We are all going to gather our things

01:16:05.340 --> 01:16:08.520
and follow the band,
marching to Phelps Gate,

01:16:08.520 --> 01:16:11.288
where the commemorative
stone will be dedicated.

01:16:11.288 --> 01:16:15.371
(audience laughing and chatting)

01:16:17.622 --> 01:16:20.789
(audience applauding)

01:16:31.478 --> 01:16:34.020
- One, two, three, four.

01:16:34.020 --> 01:16:36.490
(mellow piano music)

01:16:36.490 --> 01:16:41.490
♪ Mmm ♪

01:16:43.954 --> 01:16:48.954
♪ When you're down and troubled ♪

01:16:49.877 --> 01:16:54.877
♪ And you need a helping hand ♪

01:16:55.519 --> 01:17:00.519
♪ And nothing, nothin' is going right ♪

